\exercise{Exercise 1 -- Components and time-series models}
Identify the component $T$, $C$, $S$, or $R$ for: a general trend, a recession-related movement, a recurring quarterly peak, and an exceptional unpredictable shock. Write the complete additive and multiplicative models. State the simplification used later in the course when cyclical and residual components are ignored.
\exercise{Exercise 2 -- Centred moving average of order 4}
For quarterly sales $18,26,20,35,25,36,28,48$, calculate all simple 4-term moving averages, then centre them to obtain centred moving averages at periods 3 to 6. Explain why an even-order moving average must be centred.
