Use the multiplicative model and trend $T(t)=3t+15.40$, with $t=1$ for Q1 2012. Calculate the first two seasonal ratios, explain quarterly seasonal averaging, correct the rounded seasonal means $0.90,1.15,0.81,1.25$ so that their mean is 1, and forecast 2015 ($t=13$ to 16), both deseasonalised and seasonalised.

