\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 1}
General trend $\to T$; recession movement $\to C$; recurring peak $\to S$; exceptional shock $\to R$.
\[
\boxed{Y=T+C+S+R}\quad\text{(additive)},
\]
\[
\boxed{Y=T\times C\times S\times R}\quad\text{(multiplicative)}.
\]
Later in the course, $C=R=0$ in the additive model and $C=R=1$ in the multiplicative model.
\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 2}
Simple 4-term moving averages are $24.75,26.50,29.00,31.00,34.25$.
Centred values are
\[
(24.75+26.50)/2=\boxed{25.625},
\]
\[
(26.50+29.00)/2=\boxed{27.75},\quad(29+31)/2=\boxed{30.00},
\]
\[
(31+34.25)/2=\boxed{32.625}.
\]
An even-order simple moving average falls between two periods, so it must be centred.
\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 3}
$T_1=18.4$ and $T_2=21.4$. Therefore
\[
S_1=18/18.4=0.978\approx0.98,\quad S_2=26/21.4=1.215\approx1.21.
\]
Seasonal ratios are averaged by quarter. The rounded means sum to $4.11$, so their mean is $1.0275$. Corrected coefficients are
\[
\boxed{0.87591,\ 1.11922,\ 0.78832,\ 1.21655}.
\]
Forecasts:
\begin{center}\begin{tabular}{crrr}\toprule$t$&Trend&Seasonal coefficient&Seasonalised forecast\\\midrule13&54.4&0.87591&47.65\\14&57.4&1.11922&64.24\\15&60.4&0.78832&47.61\\16&63.4&1.21655&77.13\\\bottomrule\end{tabular}\end{center}
The deseasonalised forecast is simply the trend value.

